  abstract = {In this essay, changing times will be center stage – from Euro-American colonization to contemporary American imperialism, from the ideal use of rule of law to its use as protection for American imperialism, from post-colonialism to new states, from what it means to be colonized to what it means to “lack” a rule of law tradition. All of these functions are associated with war or peace, with plunder or its opposite, both good and bad functions, which challenge the generally acceptable position that rule of law is a good thing with no dark side. When we recognize the dark side, that is, the lawlessness allowed by law, should we ask if Rule of Law is now a myth – something that exists in the imagination functioning as a controlling process.},
